      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Please do not adjust your dosage without speaking to your doctor first, as this is a medical decision. Lightheadedness when standing up is a common side effect of blood pressure medication, often called orthostatic hypotension, and your doctor can advise on managing it. If this symptom is bothersome, contact your prescribing physician to discuss whether a dose change or timing adjustment is appropriate for you.",
      "source": "target",
